{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 10, "variables": 4, "prime": 2013265921, "coeff_bound": 2013265920}, "seed": 1411684335, "solved": "failed", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": false, "verify_reason": "circuit_2_is_not_proportional_to_weight_row_2", "reply": "To find the compact lexicographic Gr\u00f6bner basis, we determine the hidden scalars $a_1, a_2, a_3 \\in \\text{GF}(p)$ (with $p = 2013265921$) defining the linear forms of each circuit $g_i(x) = (\\text{linear}_i \\cdot x)^{10} - 1$:\n\n1. **Circuit 0 ($i=0$):**\n   - $\\text{linear} = [1, 0, 0, 0]$\n\n2. **Circuit 1 ($i=1$):**\n   - $\\text{weights}[1] = [1]$\n   - $\\text{linear} = [a_1, 1, 0, 0]$\n   - Using points with $x_0 = 1$ and consecutive $x_1 \\in \\{371098955, 371098957\\}$ whose difference is $2$, the values of $a_1 x_0 + x_1$ correspond to $-1$ and $1$ in $\\mu_{10}$, giving:\n     $$a_1 = -1 - 371098955 \\equiv 1642166965 \\pmod p$$\n   - $\\text{linear} = [1642166965, 1, 0, 0]$\n\n3. **Circuit 2 ($i=2$):**\n   - $\\text{weights}[2] = [1, 28]$\n   - $\\text{linear} = [a_2, 28 a_2 \\bmod p, 1, 0]$\n   - From the points with difference $2$ in $x_2$, we obtain:\n     $$a_2 = 1757151009$$\n   - $28 a_2 \\bmod p = 28 \\times 1757151009 \\bmod p = 918777521$\n   - $\\text{linear} = [1757151009, 918777521, 1, 0]$\n\n4. **Circuit 3 ($i=3$):**\n   - $\\text{weights}[3] = [1, 24, 6]$\n   - $\\text{linear} = [a_3, 24 a_3 \\bmod p, 6 a_3 \\bmod p, 1]$\n   - From the points with difference $2$ in $x_3$, we obtain:\n     $$a_3 = 226898407$$\n   - $24 a_3 \\bmod p = 24 \\times 226898407 \\bmod p = 1419029926$\n   - $6 a_3 \\bmod p = 6 \\times 226898407 \\bmod p = 1361390442$\n   - $\\text{linear} = [226898407, 1419029926, 1361390442, 1]$\n\n<answer>{\"basis\":[{\"linear\":[1,0,0,0],\"power\":10,\"constant\":2013265920},{\"linear\":[1642166965,1,0,0],\"power\":10,\"constant\":2013265920},{\"linear\":[1757151009,918777521,1,0],\"power\":10,\"constant\":2013